cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ZTARE: A filesystem-first socio-technical research system for testing claims, surfacing failure modes, and governing AI-assisted research"
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite the specific paper or artifact you are
  using rather than the repository as a monolith. The README's Citation
  section enumerates the per-paper BibTeX entries. The repository-level
  citation below is provided for tooling that requires a single `CITATION.cff`
  (for example GitHub's "Cite this repository" widget and Zenodo's DOI
  minting).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alami
    given-names: Daniel
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparckix/ztare"
url: "https://github.com/sparckix/ztare"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/sparckix/ztare/blob/main/LICENSES.md"
keywords:
  - adversarial validation
  - reflexive engineering
  - agentic engineering patterns
  - LLM-assisted research
  - research integrity
  - epistemic discipline
  - governance gates
preferred-citation:
  type: generic
  title: "ZTARE: per-artifact citations"
  authors:
    - family-names: Alami
      given-names: Daniel
  year: 2026
  notes: >-
    The repository is a portfolio of distinct research artifacts. Cite the
    specific paper or artifact you are using (Cognitive Camouflage,
    Adversarial Precedent Memory, Contract-Governed Adversarial Evaluator
    Hardening, The Cognitive Firm). The BibTeX entries are listed in the
    Citation section of the repository README.
